  "id": "COMPOUND:18835 - PROTEIN:2641",
  "verbalization": "Epifriedelin is implicated in the targeting of multiple proteins, including Tyrosine--tRNA ligase and Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which in turn target the EDD domain protein, DegV family. This suggests that Epifriedelin may act as a modulator of pathways involving these proteins, potentially through a common downstream effect on the EDD domain protein. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Epifriedelin influences the activity or expression of these target proteins, which then interact with the EDD domain protein, possibly through shared regulatory mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Epifriedelin in modulating cellular processes that involve the EDD domain protein, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
